      <dc:description>
        <rdf:Alt>
          <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">&lt;p&gt;She'd wanted to argue with her father, to oppose the annulment until she was blue in the face, but she couldn't. Not without knowing if this is what Catra wants.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;"So ... that's it then?" Catra shakes her head, lips pursed. "We're married and then tomorrow we aren't?"&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Adora clenches her hands, her stomach rolling with nausea at the thought. "If that's what you want." She tries to meet Catra's eyes, but itâ€™s too hard. "You don't have to be here against your will."&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Perhaps sheâ€™s being unfair. Adora didnâ€™t have to move to a new land full of strangers. She got to keep her life exactly as it was save for their union. If Catra wishes for her life in Halfmoonâ€”the life sheâ€™s always knownâ€”Adora will have to find it in herself not to blame her for it.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;It doesnâ€™t make it an easy task. Adora almost feels like she's not in her own bodyâ€”like she's floating above them in the moment, watching as this precious, tender thing she thought she had collapses before her.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;She flinches when she feels Catra's hand on her own, not expecting it. She raises her gaze from the lush carpet to find Catra's eyes full of tears. "What if I don't want that? What if I wanted to stay?"&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;OR Sequel to Accede the Throne.&lt;/p&gt;</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Alt>
      </dc:description>
